cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite it as below."
title: "rotor-23: a Lean 4 formalization of Eulerian walkers on Z^2 have range exponent 2/3"
abstract: >-
  A machine-checked Lean 4 / mathlib formalization of the paper "Eulerian
  walkers on Z^2 have range exponent 2/3" (Bou-Rabee and Peres): recurrence,
  the limit shape and the range exponent 2/3 of the rotor walk with
  independent uniform initial rotors on the square lattice and on doubly
  periodic plane graphs of maximum degree three (Theorem 1.1), their
  extension to rotor laws close to uniform (Proposition 1.2), and a doubly
  periodic graph on which the walk is transient (Proposition 1.3).  Six
  results the paper cites without proof are taken as explicit hypotheses.
  The development contains no sorry and no custom axiom.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bou-Rabee
    given-names: Ahmed
keywords:
  - Lean
  - mathlib
  - formal verification
  - rotor walk
  - rotor-router
  - probability
license: Apache-2.0
# Add a Zenodo DOI here once an archived release is minted.
